From 1708bbd554a08c47c6726346450988b6dffee4d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:13:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 057/152] power: supply: max17042: Handle a missing or deferred
 IRQ on platform probe

When the fuel gauge is instantiated as an MFD cell (MAX77705 through
simple-mfd-i2c), max17042_platform_probe() hands whatever
platform_get_irq() returned straight to max17042_probe(), which only
tests it for non-zero. A negative errno therefore reaches
devm_request_threaded_irq(), fails with "Failed to get IRQ", and the
gauge silently runs without alerts. That includes -EPROBE_DEFER when
the interrupt parent's domain is not registered yet.

Use platform_get_irq_optional(), propagate -EPROBE_DEFER and treat any
other error as "no interrupt", like the I2C path does with irq == 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index 505a68c26..d6d7f4278 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -1595,7 +1595,11 @@ static int max17042_platform_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	device_set_of_node_from_dev(dev, dev->parent);
 
 	id = platform_get_device_id(pdev);
-	irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
+	irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);
+	if (irq == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+		return irq;
+	if (irq < 0)
+		irq = 0;
 
 	return max17042_probe(i2c, dev, irq, id->driver_data);
 }
